 "top": "qfd_tt_ctlm_dv_lpf",
 "why": "HF-4 (HARD-FIX 0id) 10-18: Qwen TT control cluster qfd_tt_ctlm_dv (slot 777.6 x 345.6) as a landed parent. The hard TT head h16c/h17 (ck_head TT insertion ~355 ps, FF ~292) and the calendar's 2 x 64x512 SRAMs + pin registers (macro clock entry ~0 ps) differ by >300 ps and sit ~400 um apart, so they get their own clock regions: core = u_gi (W, calendar SRAMs, pin registers), hr = u_hr + u_go + u_thru (E). Every input lands from core (port_regions) and every output leaves hr, so the cluster is the flat block + 3 edges on every output (uniform). MU-ADOPT-CTLM 10-19: u_gi calendar = qfd_dv_cmd_cal_mu NU 4 (Qwen ROM 4 users) + dh_user input (core). MU-QW-DIE 10-19: OPSEG 1 (MU-QW-B1 op-start leaf u_gi.g_op.u_leaf (core), ROM 4096x72 inside; coordinator 0ka boot context record DW5/DW6 in u_gi) + QW-DIEFIX hr pack in u_thru (zero logic, hr region).",
